Package: simdfuse
Type: Package
Title: Fused SIMD Evaluation of Array Expressions and Parallel Skeletons
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Bogdan", "Oancea", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "bogdan.oancea@gmail.com")
Description: Evaluates elementwise R expressions in a single pass over the
    data, keeping every intermediate value inside a cache-resident block
    instead of allocating a temporary vector per operation. Expressions are
    compiled to a compact instruction stream and executed by a kernel that is
    built once per instruction set (AVX-512, AVX2 with FMA, SSE2, NEON and a
    scalar fallback) and selected at run time from the host's reported
    features, so one binary vectorises on whatever hardware it finds.
    Reductions are fused with the expression and therefore run in constant
    auxiliary memory, and their parallel form is deterministic in the thread
    count. Also provides parallel algorithmic skeletons for which base R has no
    construct: an associative prefix scan (including a numerically stable
    log-domain scan), a weighted stencil, and reduction within contiguous
    segments, each consuming an expression rather than a materialised vector.
    Elementary functions default to the platform library one lane at a time,
    which reproduces base R bit for bit; an optional faster mode uses
    vectorised polynomial approximations with documented, measured error.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
